    art: 
    arrival: 'Lady Ashworth: A room with a mirror. The highest you have.

      And
      keep that dreadful poltergeist away from my wall.'
    story:
    - 'Lady Ashworth: Hmph. Adequate. My portrait used to hang in this very hall,
      you know.'
    - 'Lady Ashworth[sad]: The mirror shows a hat I was buried in. I never liked
      that hat.'
    - 'Lady Ashworth[happy]: I''ve decided I quite like it after all. How freeing,
      to be wrong.'
    checkout: 'Lady Ashworth[happy]: Keep my hatpin. Ladies must look after one another.'
